On Fri, 3 Mar 2006, Hojita Discordia wrote:
>
> On Fri, 03 Mar 2006 02:27:18 -0500, Arthur J. O'Dwyer wrote:
>>
>>      * Invisibility. Shopkeepers and uniques will not wear this ring, and
>> it is not preferred when the player can see invisible.
>>      * Teleportation. Shopkeepers and uniques will not wear this ring. It
>> confers the same teleportation effect as being a tengu.
>
> In the same vein as others who asked why not regeneration, I'll ask why
> not invisibility and teleportation too? It probably wouldn't make any
> sense for friendly shopkeepers or uniques to use them, but they seem
> like they should be fair game for the hostile ones.

   Hmm. I'll admit I didn't think of hostile shopkeepers, and agree
invisibility would be a good idea for them. Not teleportation, though --- 
they're trying to catch you, and random teleports would interfere with 
that.
   As for uniques, that's where my inexperience with the mid-to-late-game 
kicks in. I'm under the impression that invisibility wouldn't do anything 
useful for late-game uniques, because the player will have See Invisible 
by then; and teleportation might actively interfere with whatever 
spellcasting strategies the uniques already use. We wouldn't want a quest 
nemesis randomly teleporting off the stairs, for example.
   It occurs to me that I never did anything to prevent friendlies from 
equipping rings of invisibility; I should do something about that.

Thanks for the ideas!

-Arthur


